 ## Overview
-Structure-from-Motion (SfM) is a traditional image-based reconstruction pipeline that estimates camera parameters (extrinsics and intrinsics) to build sparse and dense point clouds, followed by mesh generation and texture extraction [S1, S2]. It solves the problem of recovering 3D geometry and camera poses from a set of uncalibrated photographs, providing the essential spatial prior for subsequent neural rendering methods like NeRF and Gaussian Splatting [S3][S4, unofficial]. Unlike its siblings, [Canonical Frame Estimation via Facial Landmarks](16399-canonical-frame-estimation-via-facial-landmarks.md) which anchors to semantic features, and [Deep Image Matching Initialization](16400-deep-image-matching-initialization.md) which uses learned backbones, SfM relies on traditional geometry-based multi-view stereo techniques, such as SIFT feature matching and RANSAC verification, to produce explicit geometry [S1, S2][S4, unofficial].
+Structure-from-Motion (SfM) is a traditional image-based reconstruction pipeline that estimates camera parameters (extrinsics and intrinsics) to build sparse and dense point clouds, followed by mesh generation and texture extraction [S1, S2]. It solves the problem of recovering 3D geometry and camera poses from a set of uncalibrated photographs, providing the essential spatial prior for subsequent neural rendering methods like NeRF and Gaussian Splatting [S3][S4, unofficial]. Unlike its siblings, [Canonical Frame Estimation via Facial Landmarks](16399-canonical-frame-estimation-via-facial-landmarks.md) which anchors to semantic features, and [Deep Image Matching Initialization](16400-deep-image-matching-initialization.md) which uses learned backbones, SfM relies on traditional geometry-based multi-view stereo techniques, such as SIFT feature matching and RANSAC verification, to produce explicit geometry [S1][S4, unofficial].
 
